    55578,
    '### GRANT OPTION

Indicates that the principal will also be given the ability to grant the specified permission to other
principals.
AS granting_principal
Specifies a principal from which the principal executing this query derives its right to grant the
permission. One of the following:
database user
database role
application role
database user mapped to a Windows login
database user mapped to a Windows group
database user mapped to a certificate
database user mapped to an asymmetric key
database user not mapped to a server principal.
A schema is a database-level securable contained by the database that is its parent in the
permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be granted on a
schema are listed below, together with the more general permissions that include them by
implication.
Schema permission Implied by schema permission Implied by database permission',
    '{"section": "GRANT OPTION", "page_anchor": "PAGE 30494", "char_length": 901}'::jsonb,
