REVOKE Availability Group Permissions
(Transact-SQL)
Applies to:  SQL Server  Azure SQL Database  Azure SQL Managed Instance  SQL
database in Microsoft Fabric
Revokes permissions on an Always On availability group.
 Transact-SQL syntax conventions
syntaxsql
permission
Specifies a permission that can be revoked on an availability group. For a list of the permissions,
see the Remarks section later in this topic.
ON AVAILABILITY GROUP ::availability_group_name
Specifies the availability group on which the permission is being revoked. The scope qualifier (::)
is required.
{ FROM | TO } <server_principal> Specifies the SQL Server login to which the permission is being
revoked.
SQL_Server_login
Specifies the name of a SQL Server login.
Syntax
REVOKE [ GRANT OPTION FOR ] permission  [ ,...n ]   
    ON AVAILABILITY GROUP :: availability_group_name  
