    '### VIEW DEFINITION CONTROL VIEW DEFINITION

A database role is a database-level securable contained by the database that is its parent in the
permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be revoked on a
database role are listed in the following table, together with the more general permissions that
include them by implication.
