REVOKE Server Permissions (Transact-SQL)
Applies to:  SQL Server  Azure SQL Managed Instance
Removes server-level GRANT and DENY permissions.
 Transact-SQL syntax conventions
syntaxsql
permission
Specifies a permission that can be granted on a server. For a list of the permissions, see the
Remarks section later in this topic.
{ TO | FROM } <grantee_principal> Specifies the principal from which the permission is being
revoked.
AS <grantor_principal> Specifies the principal from which the principal executing this query
derives its right to revoke the permission.
Syntax
REVOKE [ GRANT OPTION FOR ] permission  [ ,...n ]   
