    '### VIEW DEFINITION CONTROL VIEW DEFINITION

A Service Broker route is a database-level securable that is contained by the database that is its
parent in the permissions hierarchy. The most specific and limited permissions that can be
revoked on a Service Broker route are listed in the following table, together with the more
general permissions that include them by implication.
Service Broker route
permission
Implied by Service Broker route
permission
Implied by database
