    '### SQL

BEGIN DIALOG CONVERSATION (Transact-SQL)
GET CONVERSATION GROUP (Transact-SQL)
END CONVERSATION (Transact-SQL)
sys.conversation_groups (Transact-SQL)
sys.conversation_endpoints (Transact-SQL)
Permissions
Examples
DECLARE @conversation_handle UNIQUEIDENTIFIER,  
        @conversation_group_id UNIQUEIDENTIFIER ;  

SET @conversation_handle =  
    <retrieve conversation handle from database> ;  
SET @conversation_group_id =  
    <retrieve conversation group ID from database> ;  

MOVE CONVERSATION @conversation_handle TO @conversation_group_id ;  
See Also

<!-- PAGE 30658 -->

RECEIVE (Transact-SQL)
Article • 09/03/2024
Applies to:  SQL Server  Azure SQL Managed Instance
Retrieves one or more messages from a queue. Depending on the retention setting for the
queue, either removes the message from the queue or updates the status of the message in
the queue.
 Transact-SQL syntax conventions
syntaxsql
Specifies that the RECEIVE statement waits for a message to arrive on the queue, if no
messages are currently present.
Specifies the maximum number of messages to be returned. If this clause is not specified, all
messages are returned that meet the statement criteria.
