INSERT INTO document_chunks (id, source_file, chunk_index, content, metadata, embedding)
VALUES (
    'chunk_65333fc80fca',
    'converted_sql-sql-server-ver17.md',
    57157,
    '### XML

Although constructing elements from constant expressions, as shown in this example, is useful,
the true power of this XQuery language feature is the ability to construct XML that dynamically
extracts data from a database. You can use curly braces to specify query expressions. In the
resulting XML, the expression is replaced by its value. For example, the following query
constructs a <NewRoot>  element with one child element (<e> ). The value of element <e>  is
