VALUES (
    'chunk_fd5119d9fb89',
    'converted_sql-sql-server-ver17.md',
    57193,
    '### SQL

<a xmlns="a">
  <b xmlns="" />
</a>
DECLARE @x AS XML;
SET @x = ''<x>5</x>'';
```sql
SELECT @x.query(''
```

  <x:a xmlns:x="a">
    <b/>
  </x:a>'');
<x:a xmlns:x="a">
  <b />
</x:a>
DECLARE @x AS XML;
SET @x = ''<x>5</x>'';
```sql
SELECT @x.query(''
```

  <x:a xmlns:x="a">
    <b xmlns:x=""/>
  </x:a>'');

<!-- PAGE 30930 -->

Creating a new namespace prefix in this way overrides any preexisting namespace declaration
for this prefix. For example, the namespace declaration, AWMI="https://someURI" , in the query
