<!-- PAGE 31027 -->

Functions on String Values - lower-case
Article • 08/10/2023
Applies to:  SQL Server
The lower-case function converts each character in $arg to its lower case equivalent. The
Microsoft Windows binary case conversion for Unicode code points specifies how characters
are converted to lower case. This standard is not identical to the mapping for Unicode code
point standard.
Term Definition
$arg The string value to be converted to lower case.
If the value of $arg is empty, a zero length string is returned.
The following example changes the input string ''abcDEF!@4'' to lower case.
Syntax

fn:lower-case($arg as xs:string?) as xs:string  
Arguments
ﾉ Expand table
Remarks
Examples
A. Changing a string to lower case
DECLARE @x xml = N''abcDEF!@4'';  
```sql
SELECT @x.value(''fn:lower-case(/text()[1])'', ''nvarchar(10)'');  
```


<!-- PAGE 31028 -->

Here''s the result set.
