<!-- PAGE 31030 -->

Functions on String Values - upper-case
Article • 08/10/2023
Applies to:  SQL Server
This function converts each character in $arg to its upper case equivalent. The Microsoft
Windows binary case conversion for Unicode code points specifies how characters are
converted to upper case. This standard is different than the mapping for Unicode standard
code point standard.
Term Definition
$arg The string value to be converted to upper case.
If the value of $arg is empty, a zero length string is returned.
The following example changes the input string ''abcDEF!@4'' to upper case.
Syntax

fn:upper-case($arg as xs:string?) as xs:string  
Arguments
ﾉ Expand table
Remarks
Examples
A. Changing a string to upper case
DECLARE @x xml = N''abcDEF!@4'';  
```sql
SELECT @x.value(''fn:upper-case(/text()[1])'', ''nvarchar(10)'');  
```


<!-- PAGE 31031 -->

This example shows how to use the upper-case function to perform a case-insensitive search.
