INSERT INTO document_chunks (id, source_file, chunk_index, content, metadata, embedding)
VALUES (
    'chunk_f385df1b7899',
    'converted_sql-sql-server-ver17.md',
    57298,
    '### SQL

Note the following considerations from the previous query:
The namespace  keyword in the XQuery prolog defines a namespace prefix that is used in
the query body.
The query body constructs the required XML.
Examples
A. Query catalog descriptions to find products and weights
<Product ProductModelID="...">
  <Weight>...</Weight>
</Product>
```sql
SELECT CatalogDescription.query(''
```

declare namespace p1="https://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-
works/ProductModelDescription";
  <Product  ProductModelID="{ (/p1:ProductDescription/@ProductModelID)[1] }">
     {
       /p1:ProductDescription/p1:Specifications/Weight
     }
  </Product>
'') AS Result
FROM Production.ProductModel
WHERE CatalogDescription IS NOT NULL;

<!-- PAGE 31074 -->

In the WHERE  clause, the exist()  method is used to find only rows that contain product
catalog descriptions. That is, the XML that contains the <ProductDescription>  element.
