    '### XML

```sql
SELECT CatalogDescription.query(''  
```

     declare namespace p1="https://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-
works/ProductModelDescription";  
     <ProductModel ProductModelID= "{ data( (/p1:ProductDescription/@ProductModelID)
[1] ) }"  
                   ProductModelName = "{ data( 
(/p1:ProductDescription/@ProductModelName)[1] ) }" >  
       {  
         for $F in /p1:ProductDescription/p1:Features  
         return   
           $F/*[position() <= 2]   
       }  
     </ProductModel>  
      '') as x  
FROM Production.ProductModel  
where ProductModelID=19  
<ProductModel ProductModelID="19" ProductModelName="Mountain 100">  
 <p1:Warranty   
  xmlns:p1="https://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-
works/ProductModelWarrAndMain">  
  <p1:WarrantyPeriod>3 year</p1:WarrantyPeriod>  
  <p1:Description>parts and labor</p1:Description>  
 </p1:Warranty>  
 <p2:Maintenance   
  xmlns:p2="https://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-
works/ProductModelWarrAndMain">  
  <p2:NoOfYears>10</p2:NoOfYears>  
  <p2:Description>maintenance contact available through your dealer   
            or any AdventureWorks retail store.  
  </p2:Description>  
 </p2:Maintenance>  
</ProductModel>   

<!-- PAGE 31089 -->

For a product model, this query returns the first two tools used at the first work center location in
the sequence of work center locations in the manufacturing process. The query is specified
against the manufacturing instructions stored in the Instructions column of the
Production.ProductModel table.',
